  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will return to the area for the next several\ndays bringing back the heat. A Heat Advisory has replaced the\nExtreme Heat Watch and has been issued for the entire area \nstarting 1 PM Saturday and ending 7 PM Tuesday for heat index\nvalues up to 110 degrees possible. The Heat Advisory may be \nextended in time, if needed. There may also be a few counties\nover SE KS/SW MO that will need an Extreme Heat Warning as the\nridge parks over us and cranks up the heat a bit higher in those\ncounties. Either way, it'll be hot. Expect highs in the 90s and\nlower 100s and for temperatures to gradually get warmer through\nthe weekend and into the start of next week. Heat index values\nwill range from 100 to 110 degrees with little overnight relief\nwith lows in the mid 70s.\n\nThe ridge starts to break down Wednesday into Thursday with\nlow-end (15%) POPs moving in by mid-week with shortwaves\nattempting to move in to the area.",
